-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 46: EMPLOYMENT ACT (lines 6102 to 6127 of the text).  LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Every decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN` (the amount in rule 4 is a NUMBER and has a yes/no twin).
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words: a flat negative, a "means" definition, a condition the
--                text introduces with "if", "where" or "unless", or a period the text fixes in its own words.
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer: it is silent, its list is not closed, it limits a grant in its
--                own wording, or it points outside these Rules.  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- O 3 r 2(1) is a caveat on every answer: all requirements in the Rules are subject to the Court's discretion
-- to order otherwise in the interests of justice, even if they are expressed using imperative words such as
-- "must".  It is not threaded as an input.
-- Every "must" below that is not done answers NOTHING (judgment call QB, recorded at each site); what follows
-- non-compliance is O 3 r 2(4), which is in another part's range.

