§§ `Rule 4 -- Payment of sums recovered (O. 46, r. 4)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "Unless the Commissioner otherwise orders" lifts the duty: where the Commissioner has otherwise ordered the
-- requirement does not apply (JUST FALSE).  Where no sum was recovered the duty has nothing to attach to: that
-- is a scope limit with no "only", so NOTHING.
-- COVERS O 46 r 4
-- src:6127 | 4. Unless the Commissioner otherwise orders, all sums of money recovered by the Court under the order, after payment of the costs, charges and expenses of enforcing the order, must be paid to the Commissioner.
@ref O 46 r 4 (src:6127)
GIVEN `a sum of money was recovered by the Court under the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 46 r 4 the sums recovered must be paid to the Commissioner` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Commissioner has otherwise ordered`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the Commissioner otherwise orders" lifts the requirement
        IF `a sum of money was recovered by the Court under the order`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is stated for "all sums of money recovered by the Court under the order"; with no sum recovered the rule has nothing to say

-- The amount that "after payment of the costs, charges and expenses of enforcing the order" goes to the
-- Commissioner.  It cannot be below nothing.  A NUMBER cannot carry JUST FALSE: its yes/no twin is
-- `o 46 r 4 the sums recovered must be paid to the Commissioner` (assumed, not ruled).
-- COVERS O 46 r 4
@ref O 46 r 4 (src:6127)
GIVEN `the sums recovered by the Court under the order` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs, charges and expenses of enforcing the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 46 r 4 the amount that must be paid to the Commissioner` MEANS
    IF `the sums recovered by the Court under the order` AT MOST `the costs, charges and expenses of enforcing the order`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the sums recovered by the Court under the order` MINUS `the costs, charges and expenses of enforcing the order`
